  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 粉\ntitle: flour; powder\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-5, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 10\nradical: 米\nradicalNumber: 119\nonyomi: [フン]\nkunyomi: [デシメートル, こ, こな]\ndistractors: [料, 数, 秒]\n---\n\n# 粉 — flour; powder\n\n**Strokes:** 10 · **Key (radical):** 米 (no. 119) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n粉 concerns powder or finely divided material. In cooking it can mean flour, but the character does not require wheat or even an edible substance.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** See 米 beside 分 and imagine dividing grains into powder. This modern-shape association is not a verified account of the character's origin.\n\nThe indexing key 米, no. 119, is on the left.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| フン | on | 花粉 かふん - pollen |\n| デシメートル | kun | 粉 デシメートル - decimetre, a rare unit spelling rather than powder (rare kanji spelling; usually written in kana) |\n| こ | kun | 粉 こ - flour; powder |\n| こな | kun | [粉](../words/粉.md) こな - flour; powder |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [粉](../words/粉.md) こな - powder; flour\n- 小麦粉 こむぎこ - wheat flour\n- 花粉 かふん - pollen\n\n## Notes\n\n- 小麦粉 uses こ for its final 粉; do not replace the whole word's こむぎこ with a mechanically constructed こむぎこな. The linked 粉 article has こな as its primary reading.\n- The pinned source places デシメートル in its kun-reading field, despite its katakana loan-unit form. JMdict separately attests 粉 for decimetre, marks that kanji spelling rare and the word usually written in kana. This is not a native powder reading or a recommended replacement for ordinary unit notation.\n- A [粒](粒.md) is an individual grain or particle; 粉 describes finely divided material. [米](米.md) names rice, not flour of every kind.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1194890, 1348650, 1504770, 2072450.\n",
